I don't think anyone will.  Those boards, based on a design from
Deskstation, we're designed to work for Windows NT then Linux.  DEC
already has a working motherboard (LX and SX) and EV 6 is right around
the corner.  The hardware for the Deskstation design (aka "Ruffian") can
be changed to support native SRM, however, it is a lot of work and not
worth the effort for Deskstation, nor Samsung right now.  Also,
Deskstation has it's own Bios and it is in their interest to promote
their Bios.

