One possible reason for the delay:

Intel is under the eyes of the US FTC because of its near monopoly situation.

The 8086 has competition from AMD and CYRIX and the likes. If Intel were to go
along with Merced, it would enjoy a monopoly situation for a fair period until
the clone makers caught up. And that period might just be at the same time as
the US Govt would be investigating Intel.

By delaying Merced, Intel may be positioning itself to be investigated at a
time when the clone makers have caught up to Intel and are enjoying brisk
sales with Intel in a much lesser "monopoly" situation. Once the US govt
decides Intel is not a monopoly, then Intel releases Merced and kills off the
competition for some time.

Intel is seing how Bill Gates who thought he was above the US govt is finding
life not so easy these days, so Intel may wish to play the monopoly game very carefully.



