expect of alloca() when the alloca.h file is included.  Apparently
this function allocates space from the stack area which presumably
gets popped off as the function exits.  

So for some reason or other malloc() is behaving like alloca() when
it shouldn't be (as far as I can tell).  I want space allocated from
the heap and not returned to it until I free() it.  Can anyone suggest
either what I'm doing wrong or how I can change this behavior?

As far as I can tell malloc() has not been setup as a macro for alloca().
In addition, the behavior goes away when the code is run in dxladebug
without modifications.

Any help would be appreicated.

