  Since the system echoes your typing, you surely have correct
cable (unless you accidentally connected PC-End 2 directly to
PC-end 3). Typically MicroVAX II would have RD5x (RD51,
RD52, RD53,RD54) drives connected to a RQDX3 (optionally
to an RQDXE if more than one RD drive).

Alternatitely MicroVAX II could have a KDA50 controller and
RA series drives though most likely as an external devices.

It might even have an KFQSA adapter and some DSSI devices
attached behind that. KFQSA emulates KDA50 controller (well,
sort of) so MicroVAX II firmware does not have to know anything
about DSSI really.

If you have more than disk, you could try booting from another
disk, say

>>> BOOT DUB1

Sometimes people build standalone Backup utility on those other
disk. It just might be that the DUB0 (later seen by VMS as DUA0...)
is broken. You might also open the covers and see how the lights
of the RD disk (assuming here) behave and whether the disk makes
any strange sound.

