Well, the system should have serial port somewhere, probably with label 1.
Typically that is the console port and without graphics system should select it

automatically.

Gain access to the system via that and try

>>> BOOT -flags S

to get into the single user mode. Pressing control-P should typically bring the
system
down to console command prompt but with Dunix it does not always work.

So, power off and on the system and press then quickly control-P before
Dunix manages to proceed to far into the boot sequence.

Btw, the console port maybe DB9 connector, so you may need H8571-J
converted to connect a VT terminal into system.

