  Sounds like it tries to do the sniffer boot and first promising device is
DUB0. However
booting does not seem to work boot... (what an excellent
observation!!?!?!??!).

As for HELP, SHOW DEV etc., MicroVAX II console was pretty primitive. It did
not
have those commands. It reacts to

BOOT device
HALT
D(eposit)
E(xamine)
CONTINUE

and maybe a few others. MicroVAX II Diagnostics Monitor is usually on a tape
and can
be booted from there. Later models had MDM capabilities (or close) on the
console firmware
but not this beast.

It sounds fairly strange that system tries to boot from DUB0. I would
typically expect
there to be DUAx devices also.

