Vesa Kukkonen wrote:

> Hi
> I got a Digital VT1300 X-terminal. When I put it on and say "boot" this
> appears on screen:
>
> -ESA0
> ?54 RETRY
> ?54 RETRY
>
> etc..
>
> I'm using thin ethernet. I also got a VXT2000, which works perfectly.
> What's wrong with VT1300? I'm using a Linux-box with bootpd as server.
> Btw, will the same image work with VT1300 and VXT2000 ?
>
> And another question, can I use my VRC16 monitor with PC somehow?
>
> --
> Vesa Kukkonen

  Well, VT1300 is far more "simpler" device. It only knows to send "MOP
request with
address". It does not (by default) do MOP request with filename like VXT can
do.

VT1300 does not have "local storage" for settings like VXT does. So, you would
need
an Infoserver/VXT (Infoserver with VXT software installed) in order to use
VT1300
like you use VXT. VT1300 can also run EWS (VAXeln Window System based
X.terminal software). The usual EWS kits are only available for VMS/VAX and
Ultrix/(VAx and MIPS).

_veli





