Hello Phil.
OK.. the card should have the following links...

------------------------------------------------------------------
| w17                                                            |--
|                                                                |
|                          w16                          w15      |
|                                                                |
|                                              w6,7,8    w9--w14 |
|                                                                |##
|                               w1--w5                           |
-------------------------------------------|||||||||||||||-------|
                                                                  \

--------------------------------------------------------------------
links w1-w5..        IRQ Address select for the network interface
                     and on-board mouse interface..

                * * * * *   a           w1=irq2
                * * * * *   b           w2=irq3
                * * * * *   c           w3=irq4
   link number  1 2 3 4 5               w4=irq5
                                        w5=irq7

the top row  "a" is the mouse side..     the bottom row  "c" is the
Net Interface side..  the middle row  "b"  is the IRQ line...
So if you want to connect the NI  to IRQ7,  And mouse to IRQ4..
you would set w5 to "b-c"    and w3 to "a-b"....

the default settings are w1 "a-b"      w2 "b-c"
mouse on irq2    NI  on irq3
--------------------------------------------------------------------
links w6,7,8          Address range and memory modejumpers.

                * * *   
                * * *   
   Link Number  6 7 8  

   link w6,  if link fitted i/o address range = 300-30f
             if  not fitted i/o address range = 200-20f

   the default setting is link fitted  (300 - 30f)

   link w7, w8.    (this info is for revision E and later boards
                   and should apply to yours. (mine is rev E01))

        w7        w8        mode        start address
      fitted     fitted      64k          D0000
    not fitted   fitted      64k          E0000
      fitted   not fitted    32k          D8000
    not fitted not fitted    32k          C8000

    the default setting is both links fitted, (64k,  D0000)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
    links w9-w14,       AUI   or   Thinwire (BNC) 

                *  *  *  *  *  *   a
                *  *  *  *  *  *   b
                *  *  *  *  *  *   c
                9  10 11 12 13 14  

     for AUI option set all links to the "a-b" position and use the 
     on board connector to interface to the remote tranciever...

     For BNC option  (default settings)  all links in "b-c" position
     and use the BNC connector on the card's back panel..
---------------------------------------------------------------------
     link w15,      AUI grounding option.

     if you are using the AUI option with 9 way tranciever cable then
     remove the link.    if using AUI with 15 way cable then leave it
     in place.    if using BNC, Then it doesn't matter...
----------------------------------------------------------------------
     link  w16,     Remote boot. This option is only used if you will
                    be booting the system from a remote DecNet or PCSA
                    server, and if you are running version 2  or later
                    of the cliect software on your system..

     if you want to enable remote boot then remove this jumper.
     if you want to disable remote boot and use this card in the usual
     way,  then fit the link (default setting)...
----------------------------------------------------------------------
     link  w17.     DC - DC  Converter for thinwire.

                    if you are using AUI then remove this link..
                    if you are using BNC then fit this link to enable
                    the DC to DC  converter to run the coax drivers..
-----------------------------------------------------------------------


I hope this helps....

All The Best Phil..
-- 
Tim. Bluck.



