Mulias were running 21066A(at 166 MHz), and 21068(AFAIK)(running at 233MHz)
CPUs. Also there are Multias running on intel cpus.
Multia(aka UDB) has two console FW on flash, SRM and ARC.

:   What was the range of CPUs supported by these machines?  Where there more
: than one motherboard or base system that I have to worry about?
:   I have heard that running VMS on these is possible...  Is it?

I had heard that there was a Multia running VMS at Digital. But nobody saw
Multia running VMS outside DEC.

:   I would like to get one to run Windows NT, Linux, and VMS.  Possible? 

You can run NT, Linux, *BSD, and Digital Unix on Multias.
NT and Linux can coexists on the same HDD. You can boot NT and Linux from the 
ARC console. You need an another HDD to install DU on it, and you can boot DU 
from the SRM console.

