Hello, all,

I am the host of the AlphaNT Source and I co-host the AlphaNT mail list.  As
an ardent Windows NT-on-Alpha user, I get to see a lot of great technology,
and a lot of places where things are missing.  Several of us on the AlphaNT
mail list have tried to put together an "Open Letter To Microsoft" to express
our concerns regarding fair competition and consumer choice in the computer
industry.

No, I'm not talking about browsers.  Something more fundamental than that.

Actually, we're trying to help the computer industry and consumers by making
sure that Microsoft delivers on their promise of choice through NT's
multiplatform architecture.  This isn't just something for Alpha users -- it
is something for all computer users, especially those using Intel
processors.   Even though you may have never even seen an Alpha, they are out
there, and having competition helps to ensure that Intel keeps on pushing the
envelope, too.  All that we're advocating is educated choice and a real
option for consumers, in a way that Microsoft can best help us.  You can read
more about what we're asking of Microsoft at my website,
http://www.alphant.com/ -- just click on the big red "An Open Letter to
Microsoft".

We're trying to see how many signatures we can get in a one or two month time
frame.  When we've got a good number, we're going to send the letter on to
Microsoft along with all the signatures so that they can respond.

Thanks for considering this, I hope you're willing to take a couple minutes
to read what we've said and also join us by adding your signature.  And
whether you do or not, please consider forwarding this note on to some of
your acquaintances that you think might be willing to help.

Regards,
Aaron
