In article <6juiqm$9p9@usenet.pa.dec.com>,
hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.nospam (Hoff Hoffman) writes: 

> In article <35587FBA.8DDAC3B1@ibm.net>, Mark Reinhart <mrrein@ibm.net> writes:
> :    I am interested in getting a VAX. I have several questions that I
> :want answered.

>   The VAXstation 3100 series has a 1.073 GB limitation on the maximum system
>   disk size, 

Depending on what you're doing, this is probably not a serious
constraint.  Keep in mind that VAX is CISC, so executable files (a lot
of what is on the system disk) are much smaller than on RISC systems 
like ALPHA.  My ALPHA:

MULTIVAC> dir/gra/siz sys$system:*.exe

Grand total of 1 directory, 307 files, 204299 blocks.
MULTIVAC>

A VAX I used to work on, which contains about the same amount of 
software (VMS, DECWindows, a few compilers, UCX):

HSVAX1> dir/gra/siz sys$system:*.exe

Grand total of 2 directories, 291 files, 29439 blocks.
               ^
(the VAX is clustered with another machine).  Yes, the block size is the 
same on both (512 bytes).

Also, this limit only applies to the SYSTEM disk.  Other disks, what I 
like to call user disks, (third-party) software disks, data disks, 
scratch disks etc don't have this limit.

>   and only the fastest of the VAXstation 3100 series (model 76)
>   is faster than the slowest member of the VAXstation 4000 series (the VLC).

If I recall correctly, the VAXstation 3100 M76 (that's the VAX above, by 
the way, a nice little machine) is 7.6 VUPs and the VLC 0.9, so a 
substantial difference.  I'm happy collecting 3100 M76s and any 4000 
other than the VLC.  Both of these, by the way, are generally the only 
used VAX machines commonly available which generally command money.  
Older stuff can be gotten for free, but it's usually non-SCSI, consumes 
a lot of power and space, is really slow etc (I'm talking 10--15 year 
old technology here).  So not ideal for the hobbiest, though there are 
many people running specialised applications which can use this older 
stuff.

By the way, folks in the UK, watch this space.  I'll probably have some 
VAX and VAX-related equipment to give away again during the first part 
of July.  I'm also looking for 3100 M76's and 4000s (not the VLC) as 
well as SCSI peripherals and printers.


