wrote:

> Department of our University Library.  It is a 5 1/4 low density
> diskette that has DEC RX-50 on the label.  Does anyone know if
> this is a proprietary hw and or sw diskette that could possibly be
> recovered? If so, any ideas and suggestions would be greatly
> appreciated.  Thank you for your time!

Hi Jenny
                  RX50 floppies are single sided Double density 
(96TPI) with capacity of about 400kb. The were used with MicroVAxen, 
the 2000 in particular I remember, as well as the DEC PCs Rainbow, 
VAXmate and the DECMate.

They were used to distribute VMS stuff for the aforementioned 
microVAXen.

My main use of them is with my Rainbows. This DEC PC ran either 
CP/M-80/86 or MS-DOS and the system was originally booted from the 
RX50 system floppy.
Under MS-DOS the disk format is not 'standard' IBM format and thus to 
read such floppies on a normal PC you will need a driver or utility 
program. I use RX50DRVR which allows to access RX50 MS-DOS disks in a 
1.2MB drive A. There is a version which allows you run from Drive B: 
instead.

Hope this helps a little.. 

Cheers - Dave.



