Oops, Phillip.  You mistyped 6.0 as 0.9 !  A VLC is only slightly slower
than a 3100/76.  I hesitate to comment on other aspects of the VLC's
performance, without better evidence than my own testing, but the serial
controller appears slightly inferior speed-wise to a 3100/38 (modem data
transfer observation) but at least does proper modem control, and the SCSI
performance is possibly better too, although only one disk fits inside.
Graphics is OK, although a 3100/76 with SPX board might out-run a VLC, and
you can squeeze in a little more memory on the older model.  A VLC with
the SVGA board will save many pennies on a suitable monitor.

The best thing about a VLC is how incredibly small it is.  And no, you
can't have mine...

