Sync on green is not the issue here.  Those of us who are purists and
like to enter the system CMOS setup and do other things in old
obsolete DOS text mode need a card like the Worldwyde Avalanche 3D
card.

The basic problem here is the the graphics card BIOS has to be
customized with the monitor parameters compatible with the horiz sync,
vert sync, etc.  If not, then the system boots up with the info on the
monitor unreadable.

This problem cannot be solved absolutely by a device driver or some
other program that resets the monitor parameters to be compatible with
the params required by the monitor.  If this approach is taken, there
is a period of time during system POST and initial OS bootstrap when
the screen is unreadable.  Not nice for purposes of system
maintenance.

