labeled "Console".  I've set it up for 19,200 baud, and chosen 8 data
bits, one stop bit, no parity. I've built a null-modem cable that is
essentially straight through, except pins 2 & 3 which are reversed.
(DB9S on both ends). The back panel controls are set with the toggle
switch down, towards the circle without the dot, and the dial is pointed

to the arrow, and not the other two icons. (Arrow looks like an analog
ground symbol).

The front panel has the green LEDs lit for the two hard drives, with the

"write protect" turned off.  The halt button is not depressed, and the
run light is lit in steady green.  The tape backup has a red button on
the right that flashes regularly no matter which position you press it.

