>surplus theres no data on the drives. But I have another concern there
>is 3 RZ23's in here but 2 of them are set on the same ID. is there a
>reason for this or has someone been messing around. The system tests
>arent finding DUA0. Any help wound be much appreciated.
>
Some MicroVax 3100's had dual SCSI, one just for internal devices and
the other for both internal and external use.

SCSI devices are seen as DK's not DU (DU was old unibus drives like
the RA81 type disks). The SCSI ID is displayed as the 100's for the device
name (ie: SCSI ID1 = DKA100).

The best thing for you to do is boot the system just to the MCR (">>>")
prompt and enter SHOW DEVICE. This will display all device information
and clearly indicate if you have two SCSI busses in this system.

If you get silly or unreliable information returned then try changing or
disconnecting one of those drives.

Lastly when setting the SCSI id for drives not that MicroVAX's use ID 6 for
the controller/host, so you have 0 to 5 & 7 available.


Laurence.







