I do not know about your particular system, but on some systems, the
application of Microsoft Service Pack 3 on Windows NT V4.0 results in
Microsoft replacing the HAL code with an earlier and older version. This
has been the cause of many hangs and crashes on various machines in the
Alpha family.

Exhausting memory as could happen in intensive rendering applications
could be a cause of hangs and BSOD. Make sure that the pagefile is
substantially larger than what Microsoft set's it for upon installation
and take all steps that you can to make it contiguous.

After you have a BSOD and reboot, what results show up with a chkdsk /f/r
? It's possible that your rendering software is stomping on a system file,
as the use of FAT file system is not as robust as NTFS.

rtt

