Hello --
I've been using DEC(BEA)messageQ for a number of years now, but I have a
configuration question that I don't know how to address.  We have a
number of DEC Alpha (OpenVMS) systems on our network, and these systems
are all directing some of their DMQ messages to a central IBM box
running DMQ under AIX.  This IBM box is part of our business
(production) reporting system.  All of the systems involved are using
TCP/IP as the DMQ transport.

Now for my question -- the IBM folks would like to setup another of
their systems to be used as a (DMQ) backup, in case their primary system
(above) fails.  This "backup" system is always up on the network, but
does not normally run DMQ.  If their primary system fails, they want to
fire up DMQ on their backup system, so it can takeover the DMQ
messaging.  This backup system has a different IP address (and name)
than the primary.  

From the point of view of the OpenVMS systems described above, we would
like this DMQ failover to be as transparent as possible.  We would like
this backup system to bumplessly take over the DMQ functions normally
handled by the primary IBM system.

I have been told to make an entry in my OpenVMS DMQ$INIT.TXT file for
their backup DMQ system -- but (and here's the part that bothers me)
with their primary AND backup systems having the same DMQ group.  Is DMQ
"smart" enough to handle having two entries in the INIT file with the
same group number?  Is this an accepted way to handle a DMQ "failover"
situation?

Thanks in advance for any input.
  -- Steve Reiner

