In article <355a21d5.23356344@news.pacbell.net>, 
   wcr@pacbell.net writes:

> We have two Alpha 4100s that were originally procured for a now-dead
> project.  They were to run VMS and share 23 RZ29s via an HSZ40.
> 
> Now the hardware is freed up and we put NT on one of the 4100s.

    Shame to waste the hardware and VMS license this way, but anyway ...

>  The
> other still has VMS, but is unused.  Our question:  How can we get NT
> to see and use the disks on the HSZ?  

   The HSZ appears on the SCSI bus as one or more SCSI disks, so I would
expect NT to see them the same as it sees any other
SCSI disk. Perhaps the HSZ has not been set up to export any of the
drives yet? If you attach a console terminal to the HSZ and type
"show units" you should see a display of unit numbers (which start
with a "D" ). Each of these should be appearing on your SCSI bus as
a drive with that unit number.

