The copying of a disk results in the transposing of the SID across to a
second machine. 2 machines with the same SID cannot live in the same
domain and BSOD is the result in most cases.

Secondly, Microsoft has a tiny paragraph in their Server Resource kit
documentation I have been reading and it says that partitons begin and end
on cylinder boundries. The AlphaBIOS in our systems does not adhere to
this and so products such as PowerQuests DriveImage Pro do not work with
the drives. I am currently working this issue, trying to figure a way
around it, without success to date.

