In article <355B24A5.6966@world.std.com>, Terry Shannon <shannon@world.std.com> writes:
>>         4. In general, whats the future for the alpha?
>>            As far as i know, there are no offical statements from
>>            compaq.
>
>Indeed there are. Eckhard Pfeiffer was pretty clear about CPQ's support
>for Alpha in speeches he made at CA-World and at the DEC Unix Summit in
>NYC on May 5.

You will perhaps forgive those of us who can remember the last 6 years
for not believing a single thing that CEOs *say*, it's what they actually
do that matters, and E.P. has not had a chance to do anything yet with 
respect to the not quite yet acquired Digital.

I don't really know what to expect, but one can hope that as we wields the 
ax - and there's no question but that it will be used heavily - that he
takes the opportunity to remove the managerial deadwood.  It would also be
a good sign if he split the current OpenVMS-WNT group into two separate
pieces, so that the OpenVMS folks could spend more time on their own OS and
less time building crutches for WNT.

As for the Alpha's future, if Compaq/Samsung/AMD are serious, they will
ensure that a fully native version of Microsoft Office for Alpha is
produced - even if it means paying Microsoft to do it.  There is just no
way that WNT/Alpha will ever go mainstream without it. 

Regards,

