Bonkers Bobcat wrote in message <355984BD.17A55413@southwind.net>...
>I jus got a couple of VAXstation 3100's. Of course being military
>surplus theres no data on the drives. But I have another concern there
>is 3 RZ23's in here but 2 of them are set on the same ID. is there a
>reason for this or has someone been messing around. The system tests
>arent finding DUA0. Any help wound be much appreciated.
>
The RZ23 drives are Conner CP3100 drives OEMed to DEC.  I think the only
difference is that the RZ23 has the "RZ23" in the ID string, and it requires a
startup command for the drives to spin up, can't be jumpered for SCSI-1
operation.  I believe Conner was sold to Seagate (?) and the drive info is on
the Seagate web pages.

On MicroVAX 3100s with the dual SCSI buses its possible for 2 drives to have
the same ID if they are on separate SCSI buses.  IIRC the VAXstation only had
one SCSI bus (?) so maybe the drives were just thrown in the box.  The boot
ROM should show DKAn: for the drivbe type, not DUAn.  Were the drives with the
same IDs cabled together?  That's definitely a problem.
    Jack Peacock




