The RD5x disks are NOT the SCSI variety.  They are old MFM drives, and not low
level format compatible with PC type MFM drives/controllers.  DEC used a weird
cabling system for these drives, but at the drive end you wind up with a 34
pin and a 20 pin connector.  The RD53 was a Micropolis 1325 (70MB), the RD54 a
Maxstor 1290 (160MB).  The VS2000 had a built in hard drive formatter.

The external TK50F tape drive went in on the back of a VS2000, so you should
be able to get to the SCSI bus.  Be careful you don't get it mixed up with the
oddball wiring on the MFM disk drives, that's not SCSI.
