I have a used VAX 6000-210 that had a XMI DSSI controller and a sperate
box with 12 RF35 hard disks configured into groups of six.

Now, my problem...

I've been told that this DSSI controller has two ports, each can access
up to 8 disks each and currently I have six of the hard disks up and 
running on the first port running OpemVMS v7.1 with no problem.

The first port works perfect, I can configure the hard disks from
OpenVMS with no problems (and had to as they were configured rather
strangely from the previous owner).

I can't get the second port to recongnize the other six hard drives.  I
know they work as I can unplug the cable from port 2 and put it into port 1
and see the disks just fine.

Now, one thing I did notice.  On the DSSI controller, their are two 
seperate places on the board for two sets of resistor packs.  One of these
sets is in place and on the board, the other is not.  What's exactly
is the deal with these and if I need the second set, what value are they
so I can replace them.

My other question is, what do I have to do to get the second port to work so I
can get all my hard disks up and running?  Do I have to do some kind of
configuration to activate the second port?

I would appreciate any and all help on this matter.

