In article <6j5a50$qbk$1@excalibur.flash.net>, "warlock" <orcus@flash.net> writes:
>I want to attach the 900EF to a Multiswitch 900 as a bridge, as opposed to a
>router. The hardware has bridging firmware installed. When I view the
>switch in MultiChassis manager there does not seem to be any way to attach
>it to the hub in Lan Interconnect.  I tried turning port 7 to the back, but
>is gave me a light green connector.  I need a dark blue connect to be able
>to attach to the thin ethernet lan.
>
>Any suggestions?

You need a blue _or_ a yellow connect to attach to thinwire...

Only port 3 is capable of connecting to thinwire LAN.
Port 2-7 (yes, Port 3 has two modes) are 6-wire Ethernet LAN (light green)

DECswitch 900EE (aka DECbridge 900) and DECswitch 900EF (aka DECbridge 900MX)
do not have the 2-wire Ethernet LAN capability (dark green). And they are
only able to connect to the first 6 standard (6-wire) Ethernet LANs of the
DEChub 900 backpanel (means you have no real win in using two bridges in hub).

Ports (eg. DECswitch 900 Port 3) capable of connecting to thinwire _and_
Ethernet have another color (green - light or dark - and blue gives yellow ;-).

