Tomkins) wrote:

>So what happens if you boot in Single User mode. On UNIX that enables you
>to type passwd directly, resetting the root password and then you reboot
>back to multiuser mode.
If your DECstation is configured to boot automatically without giving
you a bootprompt, you can reset the NVRAM by setting the jumper on the
mainboard near the power connector and booting once. Then remove the
jumper and boot and you should get the ">>" boot prompt. 

