> Question Numero Uno:
> 
>         On the back of the VAXstation 2000, there are two ports, a
>         9-pin male DIN with a picture of a printer above it, and a
>         25-pin male DIN with two arrows above it.  Which one might be
>         the serial port?

They're both serial ports. There are four serial ports on the 2000: the
9-pin printer/console port, the 25-pin communications port, and two
ports in the 15-pin connector for the mouse and keyboard.
> 
> Question Zwei:
> 
>         I'm assuming that 70MBytes is enough room for some kind of
>         minimal VMS installation, maybe even DECwindows.  Assuming
>         that this is enough space, and assuming that these boxes have
>         enough RAM to run VMS, how could I get VMS onto this machine?

There are a few ways to go. You can hook up an external tape drive. You can
hook up a floppy (if you happen to have a floppy distribution hanging around),
or you can install VMS on another machine, cluster your 2000 to it, and use
the cluster to install VMS on the 2000's hard disk.
