> Jonathan
> (remove -NOSPAM to reply via email)
Greetings,
The VAX 11/750's most common failure, as I saw them, was the power
supplies. The easiest way I found to troubleshoot them were to remove
the rear panel to expose the pwr regulators and turn on the system and
check to outputs out the regs. themself. The regs. have a large red (+)
cable and a large black (-) cable going from the reg. to the backplane.
Turn on the system and check with a DC volt meter, looking for +5 on the
red cable to chassie ground on one reg. and check the other the same way
looking for +12 volts. If you decide to replace one, be careful not to
overtighten the screw holding the red and black cables to the regulator,
because it is made of soft metal, and can be easily striped.

Any other questions, pls e-mail.
Regards, Tim



