	Why of course.  Without a cluster filesystem,
	what do you do?  I know of a large newspaper in
	the midwest that keeps a spare in a closet and
	practices a drill outswapping the existing UNIX
	box.  Likewise, a very large corporation nearby keeps a spare in
	their closet also.  From a VMS perspective this is rather silly BUT
	you do the best you can with what you have to work with.

> Clusters to provide scalability which is what Digital
> are suggesting is possible with their TPC-C press
> releases are much more rare. This is also the
> case with OpenVMS database clusters. You
