Organization: Michael Austin, Inc.
Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec


It is quite easy actually.  Enable SMTP (UCX or Multinet etc...) and
send the message to SMTP%"user@domain.address.whatever".  If you
need to set a FORWARD in VMS Mail, you enter it like:

Mail> send
To: SMTP%"user@domain.address.whatever"

Mail> set forward SMTP%"""user@domain.address.whatever"""

note the number of double-quotes.  I have been fighting Distribution
list problems send to SMTP style addresses. It can be a lot of fun.

We have some .com files that send it to the entire DL at one time 
using the syntax @distribution.dis.  The single double-quote format
works for these.  If you have a command procedure that reads each 
address and mails it independent of the other names, then you must
use the triple double-quote format.

Hope this helps.

Michael Austin
An Indepedent Consultant
