mathog@seqaxp.bio.caltech.edu wrote:
> 
> I have a copy of WNT 4.0 sp3 on an external disk on an AlphaStation, and
> want to move it to an internal disk, replacing the DU system disk that
> was there.

LOL - welcome to the wonderful world of NT!

I ran into this particular issue a few weeks ago, but luckily(?) for me,
the NT server in question was an Intel box. BTW - "Ghost" turned out to
be unreliable for me - I tried it on a test server, and it copied the
disk alright, but corrupted something in the process.  Several days and
numerous blue screens afterwards, I ended up having to do a fresh
installation.

To copy the system disk on the main server, I inserted the new disk,
created a system partition on it (with the boot files) and mirrored the
old system disk to a partition on the new one.  Once the mirroring
process was complete, I broke the mirror, reconfig'd the system so that
it would boot off of the new system partition, and pointed the BOOT.INI
in the system partition to the newly mirrored copy of the system disk. 
It's several weeks later, and my system is still running happily.

Brian



