rali@chicagonet.net wrote:
> 
> I was wondering does Nt run native in Alphas or only through an emulator?
> 
> Thanks,
> 
> Raza

It runs native.  You'll have to get a model of Alpha that NT supports. 
For example, you'll not be able to run NT on a DEC 3000 400 since NT
does NOT support Turbochannel.  I _THINK_ most of the PCI based Alphas
will run NT.  We have an AlphaStation 200 4/166 running NT.  It also
runs FX!32 nicely, but at 166 MHz, I'd like something a little faster
for running FX!32.  FX!32 allows you to run non-driver Intel NT
executables on Alpha NT (it performs a binary executable translation
between the Intel instruction set and the Alpha instruction set - hence
the need for speed!)

I have not done the installation, but I believe you use the same NT CD
for installation as you would use on an Intel machine.  You'll have to
make sure you have the correct console running...

Digital has just produced a BETA of the JDK 1.1.5 for Alpha NT.  Seems
to work okay, but we really haven't done much with it.

-- 
