Kevin Handy (kth@srv.net) wrote:


> Ste K wrote:

[Basically, he has a Multia running NT that crashes mysteriously.  It
has a Quantum Fireball drive mounted.]

> > The problem started when I used the Multia as an intranet server
> > running NT4.0SVR SP3. After two days it crashed with an NT BSOD.
> > Since then it's never been right. I wonder if constantly being on
> > has cooked something, these things seem to run hot.
> > Any
> > ideas??
> >

I'm not too familiar w/NT (a familiar strain in this thread?) but it
is indeed possible that you are having heat problems.  The Multia has
poor ventilation and a weak power supply.  I would certainly be
hesitant about mounting a 3.5" drive internally.  And the fact that
the problems started only after running for a while is suspicious.

So, try mounting the drive externally, and do not power the external
box off the Multia (plug it into its own socket, instead of using the
one on the back of the Multia).

Of course, this will only work if you have a Multia that has external
SCSI.  The 2.5" Toshiba drives that are installed in some Multias seem
to work ok, these are little laptop drives.  You might want to try one
of those.

Also check that the fan is working (it is on the front left hand
side).  And of course look for information from people who are more
familiar with your software, before rushing around buying
hardware. ;-)

Just another Multia user...

