My guess would be not.  The 60MHz (and 66MHz) Pentium uses 5v power, you 
need 3.3 volt for higher clocks, and split voltage (2.8 and 3.3) for the 
MMX models.

OTOH, do you really need a faster CPU?  I would think that even a 486
could easily flood a couple of 10Mbit networks, and I would also think
that increasing memory is generally a better idea than increasing CPU,
unless you do very unusual CGI or Java stuff.

(My experience is mostly with Apache on Linux, other systems may have
different resource requirements)

