No, this isn't correct.
System boards can be moved between domains without shutting down the
affected domains.

Based on what I've seen from the outside, my conjecture as to how it
works is that running jobs are moved to CPUs on other boards, then the
memory on the board being shut down is flushed to swap space; it
faults its way back in on other system boards in the doamin.

